## 2. File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) Configuration
FIM (`syscheck`) tracks creations, modifications, and deletions in critical system directories and registry keys on `Win-DC01`.

1. On `Win-DC01`, edit `C:\Program Files (x86)\ossec-agent\ossec.conf` (or push via centralized `agent.conf` on the manager).
2. Ensure real-time monitoring and `whodata` auditing are enabled for sensitive directories:
   ```xml
   <syscheck>
     <disabled>no</disabled>
     <frequency>43200</frequency>
     <scan_on_start>yes</scan_on_start>

     <!-- Monitor critical Windows system folders in real time -->
     <directories check_all="yes" realtime="yes" report_changes="yes">C:\Windows\System32\drivers\etc</directories>
     <directories check_all="yes" realtime="yes">C:\Windows\System32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0</directories>
     <directories check_all="yes" realtime="yes">C:\Users\Administrator\Desktop</directories>

     <!-- Monitor Autorun Registry Keys -->
     <windows_registry>HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run</windows_registry>
     <windows_registry>HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\RunOnce</windows_registry>
   </syscheck>
   ```
3. Restart the Wazuh Agent on `Win-DC01`:
   ```powershell
   Restart-Service -Name WazuhSvc
   ```

